etime","value":"2024-03-29T01:11:25.617091"}}},"ISBN:9781573222761":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781573222761","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL18165510M/Living_with_the_devil","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL18165510M/Living_with_the_devil","details":{"publishers":["Riverhead Books"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["2933896"],"goodreads":["2088617"]},"subtitle":"a meditation on good and evil","local_id":["urn:sfpl:31223050595207","urn:sfpl:31223050595231","urn:sfpl:31223050595264","urn:sfpl:31223050595249","urn:cst:10017040449"],"lc_classifications":["BQ4301 .B37 2004","BQ4301.B37 2004"],"key":"/books/OL18165510M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL399410A","name":"Stephen Batchelor"}],"publish_places":["New York"],"subjects":["Religious life -- Buddhism","Good and evil -- Religious aspects -- Buddhism","Buddhism -- Doctrines"],"pagination":"224 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run03.mrc:69629391:1971","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_barcode.mrc:36324003:2970","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part31.utf8:175009942:736","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_multibarcode.mrc:36337754:2970","bwb:9781573222761","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-010.mrc:309043457:3286","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.09.20150123.full.mrc:411612074:792"],"title":"Living with the devil","lccn":["2004042759"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 213-222)"},"number_of_pages":224,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["1573222763"],"publish_date":"2004","publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"Stephen Batchelor","oclc_numbers":["54479821"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL2727750W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Living with the Devil is Stephen Batchelor's work on humankind's greatest struggle - to become good. Batchelor traces the trajectory - from the words of the Buddha and Christ, through the writings at Shantideva, Milton, and Pascal, to the poetry of Baudelaire and the fiction of Kafka - of impediments that keep us from doing what's in our own and others' best interests. He shows us the myriad forms those obstacles take: a wandering farmer, a caring friend, a devout religious believer, a powerful king, even a frustrated old man who doodles in the sand when he cannot snare the Buddha. The devil need not appear with horns and a forked tail: he stands for everything that paralyzes our innate wisdom, freedom, and empathy, thus blocking our paths in life. In a world of black and white, Batchelor paints in shades of gray, illustrating what it means to live in an ambiguous and precarious environment that continually tempts us from what we hold to be good.\" \"Drawing on classic religious texts from East and West, as well as the findings of modern physics and evolutionary biology, Batchelor asks us to examine who we really are, and to rest in the uncertainty that we may never know.\" \"Living with the Devil tells a tale that weaves its way among philosophy, religion, and science, and psychology, history, and myth. This is a book that will challenge your attitudes, your beliefs, the very way you live your life.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":13,"revision":13,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-10-11T16:36:40.289001"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-12-05T15:30:41.066474"}}},"ISBN:9781594480874":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781594480874","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL19682191M/Living_with_the_devil","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/livingwithdevilm00batc","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6748813-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Riverhead Books"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["260633"],"librarything":["2933896"]},"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"title":"The God of this age","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"title":"Creating a path"